# Two materials for tetra.obj: one plain, one with a shine on it.
#
# No `map_Kd` anywhere, deliberately. A texture reference would mean a checked-in image, and
# the point of this fixture is that a fresh clone can bake something without acquiring an
# asset. What it does exercise is the part with the most ways to go quietly wrong: an .mtl
# resolved beside its .obj, two named materials, and faces grouped onto each of them.

newmtl shell
Kd 0.820000 0.780000 0.700000
Ka 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
Ks 0.050000 0.050000 0.050000
Ns 8.000000
d 1.000000

newmtl core
Kd 0.180000 0.320000 0.560000
Ka 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
Ks 0.600000 0.600000 0.600000
Ns 120.000000
d 0.650000
